# Broader community events (festivals, markets, celebrations)

## Core rule

> **Puddles includes events that give little ones something meaningful to do — not simply events where children are welcome.**

For broader community events, require at least **one strong toddler-relevant reason**, ideally two (Kids Zone, crafts, music/dance, animals/vehicles, play structures, participatory cultural activities, seasonal kid experiences, short drop-in performances).

### Usually exclude

- “All ages” with no child activity
- Primarily food/drink/shopping
- Adult concerts where kids are only permitted
- Late-night festivals
- Activities mainly for 6+
- Farmers markets with only vendors/produce

### Farmers markets

> The market itself is not an event. A special kids activation at the market can be.

## Activity type: Festivals & Community

Do **not** invent a **Family Friendly** activity type.

### Definition

Broader local events not designed specifically for young children, but with a clear, meaningful experience for little ones—something to **explore, watch, participate in, or experience**, not merely attend.

### Include when

Clear reason ages 0–5 would enjoy it; kid activities (crafts, music, face painting, animals, vehicles, play areas, demos); casual drop-in outing; **no more specific type fits**.

### Do not include when

Kids welcome but nothing meaningful for them; primarily food/alcohol/shopping/adult entertainment; stroller-friendly only; mainly 6+; a specific type fits better.

### Classification rule

> **Use Festivals & Community when a broader community event gives little ones something meaningful to do or experience—not simply because kids are welcome.**

Prefer **Arts & Crafts**, **Music & Movement**, **Parent & Me**, etc. when they fit. One primary type per event.

Full definition, examples, and edge cases: `docs/community-events-inclusion.md` §2.

## Card copy

The subtitle / Good to know should answer **why Puddles recommends this for little ones**, not “family-friendly” or “all ages welcome.”

Example: *Kids Zone with face painting, trampolines & more*

## Age wording

- Toddler-specific programs: can use best-for ages (e.g. 2–5).
- Broader festivals: prefer **All ages · Little ones welcome** (or All ages + a short “best for little ones who…” line). Do not pretend the festival is designed only for toddlers.

## Filters

Do not add a **Family Friendly** filter. **Festivals & Community** is in the Activity Type filter; no separate Festival filter.

